{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1094873-inanimae-affinity","id":1094873,"title":"Inanimae Affinity","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-20T08:38:36-07:00","id":1094873,"title":"Inanimae Affinity","content":"My Inanimae Dryad has an Affinity for Verdage Unleashings... can anyone help me with what that mean?<br /> <br /> Trying to grok this : )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1383-yrtalien","name":"yrtalien","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T02:11:22-07:00","id":1095066,"title":"","content":"I think it means you're at -1 difficulty for the cantrip roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T07:22:50-07:00","id":1095121,"title":"","content":"That would on its face make sense, however Inanimae can only unleash... not use cantrips. Lowering the the difficulty of an unleashing roll is a mixed trick since it can lead to chaos and Bedlam very easily... It was my hope that affinity, in this case, might lead to a situation equivalent to Unleashing at or near your anchor.... a virtual level to add to your Sliver for avoiding Chaos and Bedlam.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1383,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1383-yrtalien","user":"yrtalien","date":". 05-21-2017, 10:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1383-yrtalien","name":"yrtalien","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T07:47:53-07:00","id":1095127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>yrtalien</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1094873-inanimae-affinity?p=1095121#post1095121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">however Inanimae can only unleash... not use pantries.</div> </div> </div> </div>Take that Inanimae! Your kitchens will be forever cursed to chaos and disorganization since you're barred from pantries!<br /> <br /> (with apologies, I understood what you meant, but I couldn't pass it up \ud83d\ude09 )","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T15:13:18-07:00","id":1095256,"title":"","content":"I completely understand, unfortunately auto-correct made me it's bitch again. <br /> <br /> Anyone have any light to shed on the question?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1383-yrtalien","name":"yrtalien","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-22T10:32:45-07:00","id":1095544,"title":"","content":"I can only offer the House Ruled interpretation I would use in my chronicles. The Inanimae Affinities for Unleashing mean that their roll is considered at -1 successes to calculate whether or not they lose control of the Unleashing.<br /> <br /> <b>ETA: </b>Alternatively, you could say it adds a +1 to the difficulty <i>solely to calculate</i> whether or not they lose control of the Unleashing. So, if the difficulty is 7, they roll 4 successes, only 8's and above would count for calculating if they lose control.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13420-gl1tterboots","user":"gl1tterboots","date":". 05-22-2017, 01:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13420-gl1tterboots","name":"gl1tterboots","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-22T13:25:50-07:00","id":1095605,"title":"","content":"That's pretty much the houserule I would use too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1383-yrtalien","name":"yrtalien","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-28T20:20:46-07:00","id":1446404,"title":"","content":"Given that constantly Unleashing means a really swift slide into Bedlam and constant exploding nightmare dice, I've house ruled that Inanimae can't start with Realms but can learn them to give them control over their magic. 'cause otherwise these immortal beings don't really last very long. So, by that ruling, they get cantrips. But I do like the idea that it could help prevent their Unleashings from going wild also.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3988-windthin","name":"Windthin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3988_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}